{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Let the redeemed of YHWH say</b> — The Rabbis of blessed memory said: four are required to give thanks, and they are those mentioned in the psalm. And the word הודו לה, the redeemed say it; therefore after it they say: <b>from the hand of the distresser</b> [מיד צר], like <b>distress and constraint; in my distress</b> [צר ומצוק בצר לי]."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 107, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:52.478441102Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}